  internal_note = {Sepsis-3. Verified 2026-07-28 against the primary abstract (PMID 26903338), verbatim: septic shock is clinically identified by "a vasopressor requirement to maintain a mean arterial pressure of 65 mm Hg or greater and serum lactate level greater than 2 mmol/L (greater than 18 mg/dL) in the absence of hypovolemia". Only the MAP limb anchors our MAP lower bound; the lactate limb belongs to the same criterion and must not be dropped if this note is ever quoted as the full definition. Distinct from the Surviving Sepsis Campaign target in @evans2021sepsis: Sepsis-3 states a diagnostic threshold ("65 mm Hg or greater"), SSC 2021 states a resuscitation target ("65 mmHg", recommended over higher targets). Both wordings are correct in their own document; do not harmonise one onto the other.}
