  internal_note = {Standard ICU reference. WARNING [2026-07-27]: the previous chapter mapping recorded here was found INCORRECT against the 4th edition itself and has been removed. ONE chapter pointer to this work survives on purpose and must not be swept away: Ch. 25, cited at supplement.tex L217 and manuscript.md L1093 for the pre-lung-protective tidal volumes -- tidal volumes of 10 to 15 mL/kg, which the chapter says "became standard during mechanical ventilation" (that clause is the verbatim fragment recorded in commit 0472424; the 10-15 mL/kg range is reported from the same passage but was not recorded as a quotation). Located in the primary text and restored in commit 0472424 in place of the Ch. 26 previously cited. Corrected here 2026-07-28: this field claimed that all Ch. pointers had been stripped, which was never true of Ch. 25. The copy audited is the 4th edition read in primary text ("Preface to Fourth Edition", copyright 2014 Wolters Kluwer Health/LWW, ISBN-13 9781451121186, 1075 pp), which matches the ISBN cited here exactly. The titles the note claimed exist in no edition: "Chapter 5 (Hemodynamic Drug Infusions and the Cardiovascular Critical Patient)" -- Ch. 5 is "Alimentary Prophylaxis" in the 4th edition and "Venous Thromboembolism" in the 3rd; "Chapter 21 (Acid-Base Disorders)" -- that is a SECTION name spanning Ch. 28-30 in the 3rd edition, while Ch. 21 is "Oximetry and Capnometry" in the 4th and hypercapnia is Ch. 20; "Chapter 26 (Principles of Mechanical Ventilation)" -- Ch. 26 is "Conventional Modes of Ventilation" in the 4th. Full-text search of that edition also found no CO2-narcosis threshold and no extreme heart-rate thresholds, which is why neither bound cites this work any more. Corrected here 2026-07-28 (this field still carried the earlier "the 4th-edition text is unreachable" state, which the supplied copy has since superseded; preprint/references.bib was corrected on 2026-07-27). Do not add or restore chapter pointers without validating them against a copy.}
