  internal_note = {Classic reference equation for blood-volume estimation in normal adults from sex, height, and weight; cited for the standard clinical per-kilogram blood-volume range. Verified 2026-07-26 in a primary scan of the article itself (located as Exhibit 1016 in USPTO PTAB Terumo v. Haemonetics PGR2025-00077; internal PDF title "PII: 0039-6060(62)90166-6", 9 pages matching pp. 224-232). Verbatim p. 226: "The normal circulating blood volume has been reported to range from 64 to 79.3 ml. per kilogram of body weight with an average of 75 ml. per kilogram. Women have smaller volumes than men with an average of 66 ml. per kilogram." Prediction equations, verbatim: men PBV = 0.3669 H3 + 0.03219 W + 0.6041; women PBV = 0.3561 H3 + 0.03308 W + 0.1833. Applied to the atlas bodies these give 72.96 mL/kg male and 63.78 mL/kg female, against Pulse's sex-independent approximately 71 for both -- which is the paper's point. The word "modest" was removed from paper.tex in favour of the two computed values.}
